From e7ae538a3d4b273cf00b75653c21eed9ab47402e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:07:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): enter a dead-end later Outside pass by a ramp along
 the pass

A later pass of a 2D Offset "Pass starts at: Outside" plan can start at a
dead end of a split level. No lead chord reaches it from cleared stock, so
the tool disc meets the crescent of uncut stock at the full tool width.
Main enters by a helix or a plunge there. The pin
outside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock reads 332.88 mm2 of
stock cut by those later entries.

Enter such a start by the existing zig-zag ramp along the pass (3 degrees
by default), so the tool lowers while it travels the first cut. The helix
and the plunge stay the entry at every other start. The late-entry pin now
counts only plunges and helices: a ramp along the pass is a gradual entry.
The pin reads 0.00 mm2.

Fixes #3567
Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
